      "records": 329,
      "statements": {
        "blind": {
          "1": "Riding a call day for the watermaster, Wren opens one senior headgate and closes three junior ones, including her own dateless family's, while pumps run on Ninefold Flat.",
          "2": "Sent to town to verify a driller's claim against the book, Wren finds her family's date struck out in a later hand, unsigned, undated, and unexplained.",
          "3": "Wren presses the watermaster and the old ditch riders, gets refusals, and traces the strike-out's ink to the last drought's emergency ledger, kept by the clerk Ely.",
          "4": "A senior ditch runs dry mid-call; Wren rides up, finds no diversion, and measures the drillers' new deep wells taking the river's own water from underneath.",
          "5": "Ely admits which third of his table is wrong: the debt came due years ago, buried in the drought recalculation that also erased the Holt date to balance it.",
          "6": "Wren copies Ely's correction sheets; the drillers petition to amend the book first, and the watermaster suspends her, offering the Holt date back for her silence.",
          "7": "At the season's last call Wren refuses the restored date, opens her dried-out neighbour's headgate, and reads the corrected figures aloud to the assembled valley.",
          "8": "The correction enters the book, the drillers' wells take the junior date they earned, and Wren rides ditch still dateless, closing her family's gate by her own choice."
        },
        "world_aware": {
          "1": "Riding ditch in the shortage, Wren closes her own neighbours' gates for a senior call, watches water walk backwards out of their field, and hands Serrell the tally.",
          "2": "Kane buys Wren a drink on the Headgate Row and offers cash for her notebook of fifth years, mentioning that her grandfather dug the Ninefold lateral.",
          "3": "At Tebb's furrow Wren finds no moth eggs and a pressed moth-board, signs the forfeiture, and watches his cord knot cut while Kane's buyers move up.",
          "4": "Two days' ride away, Wren opens a box in a back-room register and reads her father's signature selling the Holt date to Kane, for a bore that hit salt.",
          "5": "Veck's nephew asks Wren to be the rider who speaks the old woman's date this August, her own name entered in the book beside it; she agrees.",
          "6": "Kane offers to sell the Holt paper back for her August silence; checking the register, Wren finds Veck's last three calls entered with no rider's name at all.",
          "7": "In August the nephew tells Wren the words to say; instead she writes down who has been speaking Veck's date and hands it to Serrell, voiding his calls.",
          "8": "Serrell strikes Veck's date, reads the board eleven names longer, writes Wren a junior date on dropped ground; Wren calls it, and goes dry through the funeral."
        }
      },
      "title": "First In Time",
      "world_index": 0
