      "records": 346,
      "statements": {
        "blind": {
          "1": "Sabel brokers a dead surgeon's hands on Cold Row, checks every mark against her buyer, takes her fee, and privately notes the month's donor count short again.",
          "2": "A cutter offers Sabel a climber's shoulders bearing marks she saw yesterday on a living man; she buys the part rather than refuse it, and starts hunting the seller.",
          "3": "Sabel walks the sale backward through three intermediaries to a standing order from the house on the hill; by morning her Cold Row suppliers stop selling to her.",
          "4": "Locked out of the trade, Sabel sells herself to the house as a tolerance-tested carrier, meets Lys through glass, and trades Cold Row's secrets for passage past the door.",
          "5": "Past the door Sabel finds the wash: marked parts grafted into Lys, cut out clean, the marks carried off inside living people \u2014 and Lys admits knowing for years.",
          "6": "Sabel copies the carriers' register to smuggle out; the house seals the hill, and Lys names a price for helping \u2014 Sabel's bare hand against their skin.",
          "7": "Strapped down as the next carrier, Sabel takes the master's marked hands into her own body, ruining the house's clean product; Lys cuts her loose and walks out.",
          "8": "Cold Row reads the smuggled names and the hill's trade collapses; Lys, unglassed, holds Sabel's borrowed hands on the eleventh day as they forget and begin learning her."
        },
