        "blind": {
          "1": "Sela closes a nine-day traverse for the guild, writes the angles, and pays the misclosure \u2014 one night taken out of her body \u2014 while her cord's circle shrinks.",
          "2": "Word arrives from the ford: the Orr family and four neighbours have signed a new stone, voiding Sela's nine days, and the guild orders her crew back out.",
          "3": "Passing through Ovel, Sela hunts the vanished second lane, finds her own old field-book naming it, and reads that name aloud to townspeople who recognise nothing.",
          "4": "At the ford Sela sets stones and runs angles that refuse to close against the agreed stone, and the misclosure comes back far larger than the walking can explain.",
          "5": "Sela works out that agreement itself drags ground, and that closers' paid misclosures have been settling other people's signed stones \u2014 including whichever one swallowed Ovel's second lane.",
          "6": "Sela confronts the guild, sees in its payment ledger that it knew, is forbidden to publish, and begins quietly recruiting basin neighbours to speak the guild's position aloud.",
          "7": "Sela's four recruited agreers gather at the ford, the Orrs bring a rival signing, and breaking the tie will cost one body a payment only Sela can still make.",
          "8": "Sela spends the lost lane's name as her misclosure, speaking it into the fifth agreement; the ford holds the measured position and she cannot recall what she paid."
