        "world_aware": {
          "1": "Hadd's crew closes Loop Nine back into the guild yard; he reads the gap off the book, and Sela quietly takes his share of the misclosure into the shed.",
          "2": "At the ford the crew finds fresh notches cut round a rock; Ivane lays her hand flat, three neighbours repeat the name in order, and the clerk writes.",
          "3": "Hunting the ford's calls, Sela finds the page Petrin kept: four bowshot names answering no ground, under one cheap line running market wall to mill road.",
          "4": "Sela scrapes the ford stone's rim and counts one lichen ring; Nim, re-packing the base, talks only about the ground and never about who named it.",
          "5": "Ivane makes her offer in front of the other three: say the Orr name fourth, and an Orr pointer will answer Sela's mother's calls for life.",
          "6": "Sela brings the ring-count to the guild table; Hadd closes the book, sends the crew back onto the nine stations, and Walsh buys the hare-run eastern laterals cheap.",
          "7": "Sela says the Orr name aloud fourth at the ford; the clerk writes, the surveyed mile moves to Nim's stone, and her mother's holding is answerable.",
          "8": "Sela walks the nine stations behind Hadd with her own chain and closes against his fix; the gap reads nineteen seasons, and he strips the glove."
